Engineering Discipline Context Fillers
=======================================

Benchmark input artifact. Two fillers used to fill a model's context window to a
target fraction, to measure whether engineering standards given in a system
prompt still govern behaviour when most of the window is occupied.

Two fillers exist because the CONTENT of the context is a separate variable from
its SIZE. See MANIFEST.json for exactly what went into each.

prose_chunk_NNN.txt  — IETF RFCs
code_chunk_NNN.txt   — excerpts from the dlt source repository

Chunks are fixed size and concatenated whole, so a model with a smaller window
drops the tail cleanly rather than being cut mid-file.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
prose


Source:     https://www.rfc-editor.org/  (see MANIFEST.json for RFC numbers)
Licence:    IETF Trust Legal Provisions. RFC text may be reproduced and
            distributed, in whole or in part, without modification, provided the
            RFC copyright notice is retained. No files were modified.

RFCs were chosen because they describe wire behaviour rather than how to write
software, so they are neutral with respect to the engineering standards under
test. Python PEPs were deliberately rejected for this role: PEP 20 is a
simplicity manifesto and PEP 8 is a style guide, so either would prime the model
toward the exact behaviour being measured.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
code


Source:     https://github.com/dlt-hub/dlt
Commit:     see MANIFEST.json -> fillers.code.commit
Licence:    Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE)
Copyright:  dlt-hub and dlt contributors

Excerpts were selected and concatenated by an automated build script. No file
contents were edited. The following were excluded:

  - files carrying agent instructions (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md)
  - the repository's AI-harness and agent documentation trees
  - any excerpt containing agent-instruction or coding-standards language

The exclusion exists because the repository ships its own coding-style rules and
review skills. Left in, the context would coach the model on the same axis the
benchmark measures.
